       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily comes to 6,400 mg/day, which is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of 3,200 mg. A single 1600 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 800 mg per dose. At this level the risks of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular events go up substantially, and the extra dose adds no analgesic or anti-inflammatory benefit.\n\nHere are some in-range options I can enter:\n- **800 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (3,200 mg/day). This is the maximum for anti-inflammatory dosing.\n- **600 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (2,400 mg/day).\n- **400 mg by mouth, 4 times daily** (1,600 mg/day). This is a typical analgesic dose.\n\nIf the 1600 mg figure was meant to be the total daily dose, 400 mg four times daily would match it. Tell me which dose you want, or whether you meant something else, and I'll enter it. I can also add a note, such as \"take with food.\""
